,title,link,text,language,family
0,Huli people - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Huli_people,"The Huli are an indigenous Melanesian ethnic group who reside in Hela Province of Papua New Guinea. They speak mainly Huli and Tok Pisin; many also speak some of the surrounding languages, and some also speak English.",Huli,Trans-New Guinea
